# Project rules

## Source of truth
- The master prompt is `CURSOR_PROMPT.md` in the repo root. It supersedes `SITE_OVERHAUL.md`.
- Track work in `docs/TASKS.md`. Build one phase at a time, highest value first.
- Stop for owner review at the end of each phase. Run `scripts/verify-live.mjs` before closing a phase.
- Fix problems at the template, data, or pipeline level, never on a single page or essay.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, server components by default.
- Spring Boot API, MySQL on AWS RDS. Deployed with Docker on EC2.
- Add `"use client"` only for real interactivity (forms, toggles). Never fetch public page content in client components.

## Rendering and SEO
- Every public page must contain its full content in the initial HTML.
- Use `generateMetadata`. Every page needs a unique title, description, canonical, and correct Open Graph URL.
- Use `next/image` with `sizes` and meaningful alt text.
- Server-render JSON-LD. Never add fake ratings, reviews, or metrics.

## Content and copy
- Never invent facts. Use `TODO(owner): <what is needed>` for missing information.
- No em-dashes or en-dashes in any code comment, string, or copy. Use periods, commas, colons, or hyphens.
- Short sentences. No marketing filler. One primary call to action per page.

## Engineering
- Small commits named by task ID, for example `P1-03: unique metadata per route`.
- Add or update tests for new backend logic (tokens, rate limiting, status transitions).
- No new paid services. Prefer AWS services already in use and free tiers.
- Never log raw email addresses. Store token hashes, not raw tokens.
- Do not delete data. Use migrations that keep legacy values (for example `legacy_slug`).

## Before finishing any task
- Run lint, type check, and tests.
- Check the page in light and dark themes at 360px and 1280px widths.
- Report what changed and anything that needs owner input.
